From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lpgauthier <lpgauthier@circworld.qc.ca>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:13:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 28/29] Don't export libxml2's FTP/HTTP client from php5ts.dll

The Windows kit builds libxml2 without its FTP and HTTP clients
(nanoftp/nanohttp): PHP never uses them, since ext/libxml routes
libxml2's I/O through PHP streams, and they are network-parsing code
with their own CVE history. The 49 functions are removed from
ext/libxml/php_libxml2.def, which otherwise makes the php5ts.dll link
fail. None of the official 5.2.17 extension DLLs imports any of them
(checked against their import tables).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ext/libxml/php_libxml2.def | 49 --------------------------------------
 1 file changed, 49 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ext/libxml/php_libxml2.def b/ext/libxml/php_libxml2.def
index 9557b3e34e..1566e31cbc 100644
--- a/ext/libxml/php_libxml2.def
+++ b/ext/libxml/php_libxml2.def
@@ -453,15 +453,6 @@ xmlHashSize
 xmlHashUpdateEntry
